Phase 2.5: Android in the Connectors grid + SDK doctor, on top of faac494. Both behind the 'android' feature.

Connector is a deliberate UX bend (ADR-024 item 6): user wanted Android in the Settings>Connectors grid for familiarity even though control is NOT an event source/sink. So AndroidConnector is a 'device-link' — config = adb target (serial/tcp), validate_config/health probe reachability via adb_client (analog of Telegram getMe), emits no events, rejects send(). Real tap/screenshot stays on the MCP/agent path. Registered in registry.rs (cfg-gated 'android' arm). The connectors precedent we mirrored: telegram/github hand-roll their REST API (no SDK); NONE shell an external binary or check for one — so the device-link probe is the analog, and adb_client (pure Rust) needs no binary check.

Doctor: 'xpressclaw android doctor' -> android::sdk::detect() reports SDK root/emulator/cmdline-tools/platform-tools/system-images/AVDs/accel. Built it as CLI; the EXISTING pattern for dep checks is setup.rs check_docker()/check_ollama() (JSON routes for the setup wizard) + system::detect(). Next step = mirror that: a check_android_sdk() route in routes/setup.rs wrapping sdk::detect() so the UI shows SDK status the canonical way (user agreed to standardize).

Icon journey: rejected generic phone, then hand-rolled outline head, then user wanted the OFFICIAL one. Used Font Awesome 'android' bugdroid (filled, viewBox 0 0 576 512). It's a WIDE robot so in a square 24px box it renders short/small -> user picked '40px bottom-aligned'. Implemented via per-tile render: filled+monochrome (currentColor) for the bugdroid, uniform h-12 icon row, items-end + h-10 svg for android, others stay outline h-6 centered. connectorTypes entries gained optional filled/viewBox; helpers typeFilled/typeViewBox.

Installer was built --features android (turns the feature ON for that bundle) so the tile works live; whether the shipped default enables 'android' is still an open decision. NOT pushed.
